{
 "_about": "The record dialog and the changes made to records, one way for the Python Editor and the viewer's: run by tests/test_edit_cases.py (EditorSession: find, view, set_field, set_many, revert, insert, duplicate, pending, undo, redo) and viewer-shell/editcore/tests/cases.rs (editcore::edit). Each case is a load order (`plugins`, each with its records in the tes3conv schema) and operations: [\"view\", tag, id], [\"set\", tag, id, path, value as the viewer sends it], [\"set_many\", tag, [ids], path, value], [\"revert\", tag, id, path or null], [\"insert\", tag, id], [\"duplicate\", tag, id, new id], [\"pending\"], [\"undo\"], [\"redo\"]. `expect.results` is what each gave (\"ok\", the new id, the view or pending list, the undo's answer, {\"error\": message} for a refusal, \"not found\"), `expect.journal` the queue's journal after them. The messages are part of the answer: the viewer shows them. Generated from the Python side when a case is added, and read by hand.",
